<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Ch07_P02_Where_Is_Each_Line_Used</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Here is the proof of \(1 + 3 + 5 + \cdots + (2n-1) = n^2\) from the example above, in numbered lines.</p>
<table>
<tr><td>1</td><td>When \(n = 1\), the left-hand side is \(1\) and the right-hand side is \(1^2 = 1\), so the statement holds for \(n = 1\).</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Assume that the statement holds for \(n = k\), where \(k\) is a positive integer: \(1 + 3 + 5 + \cdots + (2k-1) = k^2\).</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Then \(1 + 3 + 5 + \cdots + (2k-1) + \big(2(k+1) - 1\big) = k^2 + \big(2(k+1) - 1\big)\)</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>\(= k^2 + 2k + 1\)</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>\(= (k+1)^2\),</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>so the statement holds for \(n = k+1\).</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>The statement holds for \(n = 1\), and whenever it holds for \(n = k\) it also holds for \(n = k+1\). So it holds for every positive integer \(n\).</td></tr>
</table>
<ol class="tb-parts">
<li><p>In which line is the assumption made in line 2 used?</p>
<div>Line [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div></li>
<li><p>In which line is the fact proved in line 1 used?</p>
<div>Line [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div></li>
</ol>]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<ol class="tb-parts">
<li><p>Line 2 states the induction hypothesis. It is used in line 3, where the sum \(1 + 3 + 5 + \cdots + (2k-1)\) is replaced by \(k^2\). Stating an assumption and using it are different things: the hypothesis does its work in line 3.</p></li>
<li><p>Lines 2 to 6 are the induction step. They prove ‘if the statement holds for \(n = k\), then it holds for \(n = k+1\)’ for an arbitrary positive integer \(k\), and they never mention \(n = 1\). The base case, proved in line 1, is used only in line 7, where the two parts of the proof are put together: the statement holds for \(n = 1\), so for \(n = 2\), so for \(n = 3\), and so on.</p></li>
</ol>]]></text></generalfeedback>
